<title>USA: HL&amp;P boosting power at South Texas 1 nuke.</title>
<headline>HL&amp;P boosting power at South Texas 1 nuke.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Houston Lighting &amp; Power Co (HL&amp;P) is boosting power production at its 1,250 Megawatt (MW) South Texas 1 nuclear power plant following a brief outage for testing over the weekend, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Monday.</p>
<p>The NRC, in its daily status report, said the unit was operating at 20 percent and increasing power.</p>
<p>The South Texas facility is in Palacios, Texas. The neighboring unit, South Texas 2, also rated at 1,250 MW, was producing at full power, the NRC said.</p>
<p>HL&amp;P is a subsidiary of Houston Industries Inc.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk + 212 859 1628))</p>
